      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The most devastating social argument is that UBI fundamentally erodes the intrinsic human dignity derived from productive contribution. By decoupling survival from work, UBI risks creating a permanent culture of dependency, where citizens become passive recipients rather than active participants in society. This shift undermines the core American value of self-reliance and incentivizes societal stagnation by removing the necessary pressure to innovate or strive.",
      "source": "target",
